    "explanation": "To the rider: part of your fare is returned. The platform trip record (EV-TRIP-05005, weight 1.0) shows the actual route was 13.8 km against a recommended 12.1 km — a deviation of 1.70 km, and the record's own within_tolerance flag reads false against POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance. Because the deviation is over tolerance, POL-RD-24 does not let the tolerance rows (c) and (e) apply. The remedy POL-RD-24 gives for a deviation of this kind is the excess distance fare, and that is 1.70 km × 0.92 SGD/km = 1.56 SGD (EV-TRIP-05005 deviation distance; EV-FARE-05005 per_km_rate_sgd, confirmed by the ledger's own derived excess_distance_fare_sgd of 1.56). That 1.56 SGD is the whole of what the policy moves; your stated 5.00 SGD is not the measure POL-RD-24 uses, and returning it would be a FULL_REFUND, a value this category's clause does not license.\n\nTo the driver: I could not accept your advocate's no-refund claim. POL-RD-21 requires you to inform the rider of the deviation by in-app chat — or verbally with a recording — before or at the point of deviation. The record times the departure from the recommended route at 10:21:30 (EV-TRIP-05005 route_deviation_detected; the first off-route fix is Upper Serangoon Road at 10:21:38 on EV-GPS-05005), while your message MSG-05005-003 was sent at 10:24:30 (EV-CHAT-05005) — about three minutes after the vehicle had already left the route. The rider's 'ok noted' at 10:25:00 answers a notice given after the fact; a late notice plus a one-word acknowledgment does not meet POL-RD-21's timing limb or convert this into the 'informed and agreed' case that row (a) of POL-RD-24 requires. Row (a) is therefore unavailable and no refund is not the outcome.\n\nOn traffic justification: EV-ADVIS-05005-01 is an LTA VEHICLE_BREAKDOWN advisory on the Kallang-Paya Lebar Expressway within the trip window (09:59:38–10:54:38), and VEHICLE_BREAKDOWN is an admissible 'incident' type under POL-RD-23. But the advisory's location is on the KPE after the Upper Paya Lebar Road exit — past the point at which the recommended route leaves the KPE for Paya Lebar Road (EV-TRIP-05005 optimal_route_via and route_rejoined event) — so on POL-RD-23 it does not intersect the recommended route and does not justify the reroute: row (d) applies. I record that this question does not change the money: if the advisory were treated as justifying the reroute, row (b) — traffic-justified but rider not informed — awards exactly the same 1.56 SGD. The rider's point that both live rows pay the same sum is correct.\n\nOn competence: the contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, both profiles show fraud_flags of 0 (EV-RPROF-05005, EV-DPROF-05005), and POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is switched off (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied false), so an AI ruling is competent; my confidence is 0.9, above the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires. No fact the refund rows need is missing or impaired, so POL-GEN-26 has nothing to escalate. No clause produces a referral here: POL-NS-24, POL-NS-25 and POL-NS-22 belong to the no-show fee rules and nothing in this route-deviation record fires them."
